  "issues": {
    "connection_failed": {
      "title": "Cannot connect to {device_name}",
      "description": "The integration cannot connect to your ABB/FIMER VSN datalogger at {host}.\n\n**Possible causes:**\n- The device is powered off or not connected to the network\n- The IP address has changed\n- A firewall is blocking the connection\n- The REST API port (80) is not accessible\n\n**To resolve:**\n1. Check that the device is powered on and connected to your network\n2. Verify the IP address in your router's DHCP table\n3. Try accessing the device's web interface directly\n4. If the IP has changed, reconfigure the integration with the new address"
    },
    "datalogger_silent": {
      "title": "Datalogger {device_name} is not reporting its own data",
      "description": "The datalogger at {host} is online and inverter data is updating normally, but its own monitoring data (uptime, WiFi status, system info) has been missing from the REST API for an extended period. Its sensors will stay unavailable until it recovers.\n\n**Most likely cause:**\n- After a reboot the datalogger could not sync its clock (NTP/internet unreachable) and stopped publishing its own data — a known VSN300 firmware quirk\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Check that the datalogger can reach the internet (DNS/NTP), for example from its web UI at http://{host}\n- Power-cycle the datalogger\n\nThis notification will clear automatically as soon as the datalogger reports its own data again."
    },
    "partial_discovery": {
      "title": "Incomplete device discovery for {device_name}",
      "description": "The following devices were previously discovered but are currently not responding:\n\n{missing_devices}\n\n**Possible causes:**\n- Inverter is off (nighttime/no solar production)\n- Device is temporarily disconnected\n\nThe integration will automatically re-discover devices as they come online. This notification will clear automatically when all devices are found.\n\nIf a device has been permanently removed, you can delete it manually from the device page in Settings."
    },
    "unsupported_firmware": {
      "title": "Unsupported datalogger firmware {firmware_version}",
      "description": "Your VSN300 datalogger at {host} runs firmware {firmware_version}, which has a known bug: the live data API (/v1/livedata) drops every connection, so this integration cannot read any data.\n\nThis is a vendor firmware issue, fixed in firmware 2.0.1. The update is self-service from the datalogger's web UI:\n\n1. Open the datalogger web UI and go to the **FW UPDATE** tab\n2. Under **Remote Update**, click **Check for FW update** — it should report firmware 2.0.1 (or later) available\n3. Click **Download & Update** and wait for the logger to update and reboot\n4. Reload the integration (Settings → Devices & Services → ABB FIMER PVI VSN REST → Reload)\n\nIf the remote update is not available, contact FIMER support.\n\nThis issue will clear automatically once the integration starts successfully."
    }
  },
